# Strategy specs are the floor

Read `docs/strategies/` for the strategy you touch. A correct implementation of a losing rule is still a losing rule—do not invent “safer” exits.

**ATM straddle / strangle (9:20-style):** delta-neutral short CE+PE, **per-leg** SL, leftover wing until auto square-off. One-way Nifty that stops one wing is **specified**. Do not flatten the other leg because the first SL hit (`*-920-one-way-holds-other-leg`).

**Chase:** continuous NRML index **futures**, overnight OK, one book per index. Entry is SL-M at day’s extreme, not a market punch on the signal bar. Expiry day: flatten front at **15:00 IST**, reopen next month; new entries already use next month. `hasWeeklyExpiry` is Nifty only.

**Momentum:** long-only NSE cash rank on daily candles. Default execution is report-only. Do not schedule orders, and do not pull history, while the strategy is off. A hold-weight lock is not bought back to equal weight. Sells use open quantity. Auto rebalance claims the IST day before it sends. A rejected basket stays claimed and raises an alert. It does not retry that day. Do not clear the claim to “retry the failures.”

**Daily trend:** long-only cash on the last completed daily close, not today’s candle and not an hourly candle. Default band is 1% each side of the EMA. Buy size is floor(budget INR / that close). Apply-to-all changes only the fields that were filled and leaves on/off, pause, status, and the stop alone. A flat book does not sell. Exit size is the open quantity. Symbol off is fully dark. Pause blocks entries and still allows the stop. An immediate broker rejection leaves the symbol flat so a later pass can buy again while that completed close is still above the band. An accepted order that is rejected later stays pending and is not re-sent. Market cap on the page refreshes through the day and is not a signal. Momentum does not filter on circuit count.

Lot sizes (Jan 2026 NFO): Nifty 65, BankNifty 30, FinNifty 60, Midcap 120. Midcap strike step 25; cash quote `NIFTY MID SELECT`.
